==German==

===Etymology===
From Early New High German sane, from Middle High German sāne, from Old High German saïne, borrowing from Old French saime, from saïm, from Vulgar Latin *sagīmen or *sagīnum, both from Classical Latin sagīna.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/zaːnə/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||-}}

# [[cream]] (milkfat)

